WEBVTT

00:01.540 --> 00:03.550
<i>Please insert coins.</i>

00:05.300 --> 00:09.230
<i>The fierce fighting is over, and the big hole
in the protective wall is plugged for now.</i>

00:10.040 --> 00:12.310
<i>We finished off the enemies that got in,</i>

00:12.310 --> 00:14.980
<i>and once the wall is fully repaired,</i>

00:14.980 --> 00:19.350
<i>I figure the Clearflow Lake 
stratum village will be secure.</i>

00:21.740 --> 00:23.950
Thanks for all your work, Hulemy.

00:23.950 --> 00:25.870
How goes the transfer circle?

00:25.870 --> 00:28.790
I think I've almost got it figured out.

00:29.620 --> 00:32.100
Even if it's not fully fixed,

00:32.550 --> 00:35.890
if I tinker some more, we should be 
able to send two or three people.

00:36.210 --> 00:37.420
Ow...

00:37.420 --> 00:39.260
That looks delicious.

00:41.970 --> 00:44.280
Might I have one, too?

00:48.620 --> 00:50.140
Exquisite.

00:53.010 --> 00:57.630
By the way, do you happen to 
know where Director Bear is?

00:57.630 --> 01:01.910
I wanted to get instructions on what to 
do about that depression in the ground.

01:01.910 --> 01:06.660
Oh, you mean where Boxxo turned 
into a huge building and dropped.

01:07.240 --> 01:11.240
<i>Apparently, that hole is interfering 
with the reconstruction effort.</i>

01:11.620 --> 01:13.750
<i>Wait a minute, this shape...</i>

01:13.750 --> 01:14.960
<i>I have an idea!</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:19.970
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:22.420 --> 01:24.280
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:24.280 --> 01:26.260
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

01:26.260 --> 01:31.640
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

01:27.270 --> 01:33.230
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:31.640 --> 01:34.170
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:34.170 --> 01:35.860
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:50.060 --> 02:53.940
<b>The Clergyman and the Vending Machine</b>

02:51.290 --> 02:53.130
I'm back.

02:53.130 --> 02:54.680
Boxxo...

02:53.950 --> 02:55.700
<i>N-i-se w-or-k.</i>

02:55.700 --> 02:58.910
I'm done with morning rubble removal.

02:59.660 --> 03:01.990
I'm exhausted!

03:02.300 --> 03:04.390
I'm done, too.

03:04.390 --> 03:07.660
The air is stagnant in 
that transfer chamber.

03:07.660 --> 03:10.240
I'm about to shrivel up, damn it.

03:10.240 --> 03:12.810
Give me something cold.

03:12.340 --> 03:15.810
Boxxo, a cold one...

03:16.500 --> 03:19.630
Huh? Boxxo, where're you going?

03:19.100 --> 03:20.430
Boxxo...

03:20.430 --> 03:23.390
Come back, Boxxo!

03:24.160 --> 03:25.640
Wait!

03:24.310 --> 03:26.570
A cold one!

03:26.430 --> 03:28.430
Something cold!

03:27.490 --> 03:29.860
Boxxo!

03:29.860 --> 03:31.400
Boxxo!

03:31.710 --> 03:33.950
Wait...

03:42.210 --> 03:43.700
This way!

03:44.330 --> 03:46.700
That must feel great!

03:46.700 --> 03:49.330
Okay! Let's get in, too!

03:49.330 --> 03:50.870
H-Hey, hold on!

03:51.580 --> 03:53.100
Yahoo!

03:58.750 --> 04:00.830
It's so nice and cold!

04:01.450 --> 04:02.840
You're unbelievable.

04:05.040 --> 04:07.560
<i>Good, everyone's having fun.</i>

04:12.570 --> 04:14.820
Suori, what's going on?

04:14.820 --> 04:16.060
C'mon, get in!

04:16.060 --> 04:18.850
I-I'm not really one for playing in wa—

04:21.660 --> 04:23.360
What are you doing?!

04:23.360 --> 04:25.860
<b>Ice</b>

04:23.730 --> 04:26.670
<i>I was right to make a temporary pool.</i>

04:29.120 --> 04:31.560
<i>It went over better than expected!</i>

04:32.730 --> 04:34.460
<i>It was decided we'd hold a summer festival,</i>

04:34.460 --> 04:38.680
<i>to give the villagers and hunters a change 
of pace from all the draining combat.</i>

04:42.140 --> 04:44.910
Due to the lack of resources, 
we can't go crazy,

04:44.910 --> 04:47.890
but I thought we could
all use a distraction.

04:47.890 --> 04:51.260
<i>This sort of thing is why 
Director Bear is in charge.</i>

04:51.910 --> 04:53.710
Boxxo! Ice cream!

04:53.710 --> 04:54.710
For me, too!

04:54.710 --> 04:55.930
<i>Ice cream?</i>

04:55.930 --> 04:58.650
<i>Nope. At a summer festival, 
it's got to be this!</i>

04:59.140 --> 05:01.140
<i>Form change!</i>

05:00.820 --> 05:04.030
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

05:01.380 --> 05:02.780
<i>Shaved ice!</i>

05:02.780 --> 05:04.020
<i>I won't take no for an answer!</i>

05:04.070 --> 05:06.530
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

05:04.310 --> 05:05.860
Wh-What's this?

05:05.860 --> 05:07.550
A new Boxxo product?!

05:06.530 --> 05:07.780
<b>Press</b>

05:06.720 --> 05:07.790
Click.

05:07.780 --> 05:17.040
<b>Ice</b>

05:07.790 --> 05:11.620
<i>I can't say the quality of this 
vending machine's ice is very good.</i>

05:11.620 --> 05:14.660
<i>However! This is where my 
skill comes into play!</i>

05:14.660 --> 05:17.040
<i>Fine ice, like powdery snow!</i>

05:17.040 --> 05:20.050
<i>With lots of fresh syrup poured on top!</i>

05:20.790 --> 05:24.570
<i>You can tell just by looking 
how yummy this shaved ice is!</i>

05:27.840 --> 05:29.510
It's cold and sweet!

05:29.510 --> 05:33.530
The fluffy ice melts right 
away in your mouth!

05:33.530 --> 05:35.180
Good stuff!

05:36.400 --> 05:38.060
<i>Yes, I'll bet it is!</i>

05:38.060 --> 05:41.420
<i>I just wish I had more than 
three kinds of syrup.</i>

05:41.420 --> 05:42.440
<i>Oh, I know!</i>

05:43.330 --> 05:46.690
<i>First, some apple slices from 
an apple vending machine!</i>

05:43.440 --> 05:45.400
<b>Apples, pre-sliced
 Fresh apples you can buy
from a vending machine</b>

05:46.690 --> 05:50.300
<i>The apples and other fruits can 
be toppings on the shaved ice!</i>

05:50.300 --> 05:53.710
<i>Voila! Deluxe shaved ice!</i>

05:55.620 --> 05:57.460
Boxxo, what're you selling?

05:57.460 --> 05:59.580
Fruit and ice?

05:59.580 --> 06:01.970
That looks so good!

06:04.930 --> 06:08.890
<i>The Hunters Association is picking up 
the tab for all food and drink today!</i>

06:08.890 --> 06:11.050
<i>So, have all you want!</i>

06:11.680 --> 06:17.940
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

06:12.940 --> 06:16.140
You know, what kind of magic item <i>is</i> Boxxo?

06:16.140 --> 06:17.940
He's not a weapon or armor.

06:18.300 --> 06:22.560
I guess he'd be an all-purpose 
goods-supply magic item?

06:22.560 --> 06:24.220
That's too long!

06:24.220 --> 06:26.960
Wouldn't "all-purpose magic item" work?

06:26.940 --> 06:30.700
<b>Ice</b>

06:27.440 --> 06:30.190
<i>Ve-n-d-in mu-ch-in.</i>

06:30.190 --> 06:33.210
Huh? "Vendin muchin"?

06:33.210 --> 06:34.700
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

06:34.700 --> 06:37.960
<i>I'm trying to say "vending machine," 
but that's what comes out.</i>

06:38.220 --> 06:40.720
<i>It'll just have to do for now.</i>

06:45.200 --> 06:46.710
Hey, Boxxo.

06:47.210 --> 06:51.460
You know that guy who destroyed my village?

06:51.460 --> 06:55.930
Last night Director Bear said he gave 
him the punishment he deserved.

06:56.410 --> 07:00.800
I feel like my purpose has run out.

07:01.720 --> 07:07.010
<i>With vengeance as her only goal, she even 
became a hunter in her quest for strength.</i>

07:07.010 --> 07:09.240
<i>What should I say to her now?</i>

07:10.280 --> 07:12.110
<i>H-a-v f-u-n.</i>

07:13.180 --> 07:18.390
<i>You an-d I b-o-th.</i>

07:18.900 --> 07:21.700
<i>Look at me, reduced to a vending machine.</i>

07:22.170 --> 07:24.080
<i>It's not like I have no complaints.</i>

07:24.080 --> 07:29.010
<i>But the time I've spent with Lammis 
and the rest has been a treasure.</i>

07:29.580 --> 07:30.460
<i>And so...</i>

07:32.490 --> 07:34.480
Yeah, you're right.

07:34.480 --> 07:37.690
You'll be with me to the end, won't you?

07:37.690 --> 07:39.130
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

07:39.440 --> 07:40.630
All right!

07:40.970 --> 07:44.290
There are still plenty of things to do!

07:44.290 --> 07:45.640
<i>Hello there.</i>

07:47.640 --> 07:52.020
Hulemy and Shimelai got the 
transfer circle working again.

07:52.020 --> 07:54.160
You're amazing, Hulemy!

07:54.160 --> 07:56.450
But it's not fully functional yet.

07:56.450 --> 07:59.850
It's limited to within the dungeon
and can only link to a single location.

07:59.850 --> 08:02.790
We can only send about three people at most.

08:02.790 --> 08:08.540
I've already decided where to 
send people: the Origin stratum.

08:08.540 --> 08:15.310
Because that's the only stratum that 
leads directly out of the dungeon.

08:15.310 --> 08:19.180
It would make evacuating residents 
and getting reinforcements easier.

08:19.180 --> 08:21.870
And about the three people we'll send.

08:21.870 --> 08:23.800
I'd like you to be one, Hulemy.

08:23.800 --> 08:28.310
Yeah, because without me, there'll be 
no linking back to our transfer circle.

08:28.680 --> 08:32.110
Lammis and Boxxo, I'd like 
to ask you to go, too.

08:32.110 --> 08:37.760
With his excellent defensive and food 
provision abilities, Boxxo should come in handy.

08:37.760 --> 08:39.190
Sure, okay.

08:39.190 --> 08:42.940
I've also been worried about everyone at 
the orphanage, and the Menagerie of Fools.

08:42.940 --> 08:44.190
You okay with that, Boxxo?

08:44.190 --> 08:45.080
<i>Y-ea.</i>

08:45.300 --> 08:48.580
<i>If I can be of help, I'll gladly take part!</i>

08:48.580 --> 08:54.130
And since Boxxo doesn't have to count 
toward the limit, we can fit one more.

08:54.130 --> 08:55.330
I will accompany them.

08:57.170 --> 08:58.690
<i>Oh, Mishuel!</i>

08:58.690 --> 09:00.000
You'll go for us?

09:00.000 --> 09:01.610
And do what little I can.

09:01.610 --> 09:03.340
<i>This is reassuring!</i>

09:05.340 --> 09:10.810
I can speak to you, Master Boxxo, and 
a little bit to Lammis and Hulemy.

09:10.810 --> 09:12.860
What would I do if you all left me?

09:12.860 --> 09:14.860
<i>Ah, so that's it.</i>

09:15.400 --> 09:19.860
I apologize for sending you under these 
circumstances, but please see to it.

09:19.860 --> 09:21.240
Be careful.

09:22.740 --> 09:24.730
Okay, off we go!

09:28.000 --> 09:32.000
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

09:29.270 --> 09:31.080
<i>Vending Machine Two</i>

09:31.080 --> 09:32.000
<i>E-h?</i>

09:32.000 --> 09:35.470
<b>The Origin Stratum</b>

09:37.630 --> 09:40.610
Those are human footprints, not monster.

09:40.610 --> 09:44.140
They must have turned back when they 
couldn't use the transfer circle.

09:46.390 --> 09:48.920
Stab away with those spears!

09:48.920 --> 09:51.400
Don't let up with the arrows, either!

09:51.400 --> 09:53.730
If you get tired,
have someone take your place!

09:53.730 --> 09:55.020
Jumping in!

09:56.400 --> 09:58.310
Roaring Strike!

10:01.540 --> 10:05.880
Looking good! Now I think today's 
attack will get us somewhere.

10:05.880 --> 10:08.930
Captain! Reinforcements are here!

10:08.930 --> 10:10.080
We'd love the help!

10:11.240 --> 10:15.100
Goddamn, but are you a sight for sore eyes!

10:15.090 --> 10:16.840
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

10:15.320 --> 10:17.840
Hey you lot, food's here!

10:16.970 --> 10:17.840
<b><i>Oden
 Kokuuma
 Lightly Salted</i></b>

10:17.840 --> 10:19.640
So cold! So good!

10:19.640 --> 10:22.050
It's been days since we had decent food!

10:22.050 --> 10:23.480
I'm so grateful!

10:23.480 --> 10:26.730
<i>Look at them go! That'll run out in no time!</i>

10:27.110 --> 10:29.300
<i>Argh! I can think about it later!</i>

10:29.300 --> 10:32.490
<i>Right now, I'll just focus on 
vending product at top speed!</i>

10:34.360 --> 10:36.360
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

10:37.710 --> 10:39.600
You're seriously a lifesaver.

10:39.600 --> 10:41.800
We were close to our limit.

10:41.800 --> 10:45.380
It was almost time to think 
about worst-case options.

10:45.600 --> 10:47.480
<i>Worst-case options?</i>

10:47.480 --> 10:49.630
<i>No, I'd rather not know.</i>

10:50.300 --> 10:53.460
I can't thank you enough, my man Boxxo.

10:53.460 --> 10:54.900
<i>C-a-p-t-in.</i>

10:54.900 --> 10:55.620
What?

10:55.620 --> 10:57.000
<i>S-t-ere-s.</i>

10:57.000 --> 10:59.560
What, the stairs to the surface?

10:59.560 --> 11:00.470
Wait, what?!

11:00.470 --> 11:02.450
Are we having a conversation?!

11:02.450 --> 11:04.440
You learned how to talk?!

11:04.440 --> 11:05.140
<i>Y-ea.</i>

11:05.140 --> 11:08.000
Sorry, I'll have to update 
you on Boxxo later.

11:08.000 --> 11:11.190
This stratum has a stairway 
that connects to the surface?

11:11.190 --> 11:13.890
You weren't able to get out of the dungeon?

11:13.890 --> 11:18.500
Nope. The big door in front of the 
big stairway refuses to budge.

11:18.500 --> 11:23.030
Our only choice was to dig in 
here and fight off the enemy.

11:23.030 --> 11:24.150
I see.

11:26.910 --> 11:29.870
<b>Shui</b>

11:27.130 --> 11:29.270
Boxxo...

11:29.270 --> 11:31.030
Food...

11:31.950 --> 11:33.290
<i>Hang on, Shui!</i>

11:38.800 --> 11:42.260
<b>Filmina</b>

11:39.030 --> 11:42.430
Hardly anyone in the Origin 
stratum has any experience.

11:42.430 --> 11:46.180
Even just against all those green fiends, 
we suffered a lot of casualties.

11:46.180 --> 11:49.600
<b>Shiro</b>

11:46.620 --> 11:50.900
They might have been in real trouble 
if we'd arrived a little later, Aka.

11:50.900 --> 11:52.530
That's right, Shiro.

11:50.980 --> 11:54.400
<b>Aka</b>

11:52.530 --> 11:57.680
And we were nearly out of provisions, so there
would've been trouble if Boxxo hadn't come.

11:58.590 --> 11:59.800
That was great.

11:59.800 --> 12:01.080
I'll have another.

12:01.080 --> 12:02.720
Thanks for the food!

12:02.720 --> 12:05.480
Hey Shui, you should slow down.

12:05.480 --> 12:07.310
Yeah, that's bad manners.

12:07.310 --> 12:08.520
Sorry.

12:08.970 --> 12:10.820
Thank you, Boxxo.

12:11.520 --> 12:15.080
Yes, truly. Thank you, Boxxo.

12:15.080 --> 12:15.950
<i>Hello there.</i>

12:15.950 --> 12:18.320
I'm glad everybody's okay.

12:18.320 --> 12:18.890
Yeah.

12:18.890 --> 12:20.460
<i>I too.</i>

12:20.690 --> 12:23.590
<i>They say when the school director came 
back through the transfer circle,</i>

12:23.590 --> 12:27.230
<i>she drove off the monsters with 
a righteously fierce strength.</i>

12:27.600 --> 12:32.120
Now, once Hulemy gets the 
transfer circle working,

12:32.120 --> 12:35.800
we can evacuate to the 
Clearflow Lake stratum.

12:35.800 --> 12:37.230
Sure, leave it to me.

12:38.850 --> 12:41.480
My belly's finally full.

12:41.480 --> 12:43.980
Boxxo is my savior.

12:43.980 --> 12:46.500
What should we do after this?

12:46.500 --> 12:48.200
Yeah, about that...

12:48.200 --> 12:50.360
How's that for timing?

12:50.360 --> 12:52.500
Oh, Director Origin!

12:52.760 --> 12:56.360
It's been a while, magic 
item they call Boxxo.

12:56.360 --> 12:58.400
We owe our deliverance to you.

12:58.400 --> 13:00.760
I offer thanks on behalf of my people.

13:00.760 --> 13:04.590
Magic item engineer Hulemy,
I leave the transfer circle to you.

13:04.590 --> 13:06.010
S-Sure.

13:06.510 --> 13:09.260
This is good timing! Hear me, everyone!

13:09.540 --> 13:12.630
Right now, it is unwise to 
remain in this stratum.

13:12.630 --> 13:14.510
I think we should prioritize survival,

13:14.510 --> 13:18.260
and take temporary refuge in 
the Clearflow Lake stratum.

13:18.260 --> 13:24.120
To that end, we must protect this village 
until the transfer circle is working again.

13:24.120 --> 13:26.270
Just be patient a little longer.

13:26.620 --> 13:28.910
We will overcome this, together!

13:32.230 --> 13:38.830
Director! Director! Director! Director!

13:35.530 --> 13:40.010
<i>Director Origin seems especially 
popular with the men.</i>

13:42.040 --> 13:46.090
<i>The following day, a search party set out 
for a prison northeast of the village,</i>

13:46.090 --> 13:49.250
<i>to see whether anyone 
had taken refuge there.</i>

13:49.250 --> 13:51.610
<i>Lammis and I took part.</i>

13:52.770 --> 13:56.240
What kind of bad guys are held there?

13:56.240 --> 14:00.270
Ordinary criminals are thrown into 
the Hunters Association jail cells.

14:00.620 --> 14:04.260
But the ones imprisoned 
<i>there</i> are hopeless scum.

14:04.260 --> 14:07.290
Like mass murderers
 and those who kill for pleasure.

14:07.290 --> 14:08.300
Also...

14:08.930 --> 14:11.530
What's the status of that 
extreme degenerate?

14:11.530 --> 14:15.760
He wouldn't curb his behavior, 
so he is still locked up.

14:15.760 --> 14:17.180
What kind of person is he?

14:17.180 --> 14:18.520
A pervert.

14:18.520 --> 14:22.880
Of a rather unique nature, with many 
complaints filed by both men and women.

14:22.880 --> 14:24.540
<i>But what exactly does he do?</i>

14:24.800 --> 14:29.690
He's not a criminal, but it was partly his 
own idea to get tossed into that prison.

14:29.690 --> 14:31.300
His own idea?

14:31.540 --> 14:34.930
Anyway, that weirdo's like a cackloach.

14:34.930 --> 14:37.180
It would take a lot to kill him.

14:37.180 --> 14:38.490
<i>"Cackloach"?</i>

14:38.490 --> 14:40.900
<i>Oh, that must mean "cockroach" here.</i>

14:41.810 --> 14:44.430
Whatever the case, we still must go.

14:51.010 --> 14:53.210
The prisoners are gone?

14:53.980 --> 14:56.600
The cells are all empty.

14:56.600 --> 14:58.130
What's going on here?

14:58.500 --> 15:01.380
Oh, is there someone there?

15:01.380 --> 15:06.620
You mean you're still alive, 
you depraved clergyman?!

15:06.010 --> 15:09.470
<b>Hevee</b>

15:07.030 --> 15:09.120
<i>Huh? Clergyman?</i>

15:09.470 --> 15:11.420
I am not depraved.

15:12.970 --> 15:15.800
I simply live true to my instincts.

15:20.500 --> 15:22.850
Oh, no need to worry.

15:22.850 --> 15:27.510
I just adore well-worn footwear, 
be it men's or women's.

15:27.510 --> 15:32.370
Rest assured, I have no interest in 
the person wearing it whatsoever.

15:32.370 --> 15:37.950
How did you manage to amass such a large 
collection while being in prison?

15:37.950 --> 15:43.670
It's grown noticeably colder lately, so 
I was using these in place of a blanket.

15:43.670 --> 15:46.120
Ah, the monsters were causing a fuss,

15:46.120 --> 15:50.740
so I went ahead and opened all the 
cells, releasing the prisoners.

15:50.740 --> 15:53.880
Do you realize how wicked 
the prisoners here were?!

15:53.880 --> 15:56.200
But of course I do.

15:56.200 --> 16:00.610
Which is why I employed illusions and magic 
to attract the monsters when I did it.

16:00.610 --> 16:02.960
I thought it might benefit 
the citizenry some.

16:02.960 --> 16:04.390
You're making all this up!

16:04.390 --> 16:07.900
No, I'm afraid he isn't lying.

16:07.900 --> 16:13.160
Oh my, if it isn't Shui, my dear friend.

16:13.160 --> 16:14.660
I'm not your friend!

16:14.660 --> 16:18.280
I was wondering why I haven't seen 
you lately. You've been here!

16:18.280 --> 16:19.660
<i>They know each other?</i>

16:19.660 --> 16:22.480
Director Origin, I'm sorry.

16:22.480 --> 16:26.290
I'm afraid he's part of 
the Menagerie of Fools.

16:26.290 --> 16:26.670
Huh?

16:26.670 --> 16:27.290
What?!

16:29.570 --> 16:34.540
He's our healer, and a weirdo who's 
good with mind-altering magic.

16:34.540 --> 16:36.490
Don't misunderstand.

16:36.490 --> 16:39.710
Footwear is a mirror that 
reveals its owner's life.

16:39.710 --> 16:44.370
By looking at it, I can learn everything 
about their past and personality.

16:44.370 --> 16:47.810
I want to touch their history, 
and ponder its implications.

16:48.090 --> 16:50.820
<i>What a chatty pervert.</i>

16:50.820 --> 16:54.450
That's why I have no use 
for brand-new footwear.

16:54.450 --> 16:58.860
Give me well-worn shoes that 
tell a story and smelly boots!

16:58.860 --> 17:04.200
Those worn by hunters are 
especially ripe for my harvest!

17:04.200 --> 17:08.210
I get that you're into them, but it's 
not good to steal someone's footwear!

17:08.780 --> 17:12.330
Theft is one of the worst 
acts a person can commit.

17:12.330 --> 17:16.210
As one who serves the divine, I cannot 
bring myself to commit such an error.

17:16.770 --> 17:19.480
That's what makes this guy a nuisance.

17:19.480 --> 17:23.160
He'll go on badgering the owner 
of whatever footwear he likes,

17:23.160 --> 17:24.720
until they give in and sell.

17:25.090 --> 17:27.680
I get to have a peep into history.

17:27.680 --> 17:30.780
Naturally, I'm willing to 
pay a fair price for it.

17:30.780 --> 17:33.610
<i>I don't like how parts of him seem decent.</i>

17:33.610 --> 17:38.610
His name's Hevee, and he's as 
capable as he is troublesome.

17:38.610 --> 17:43.120
80% of the Menagerie of Fools' bad 
reputation is on account of him.

17:43.120 --> 17:47.200
Hevee, you're a member of 
the Menagerie of Fools,

17:47.200 --> 17:51.260
and yet you made no attempt to fight 
back against that monster assault?!

17:51.260 --> 17:54.330
I make it a rule not to get in over my head.

17:54.330 --> 17:57.250
After all, I am only so tall.

17:58.760 --> 18:01.370
I did not, however, just let everyone die.

18:01.890 --> 18:04.230
Time to undo my spell.

18:05.850 --> 18:11.360
By combining illusion and magic that masks 
one's presence, I put them in hiding.

18:12.620 --> 18:17.280
I wanted to save more people, but mea culpa.

18:19.540 --> 18:22.700
Amazing. I couldn't sense them one bit.

18:23.040 --> 18:24.060
Are we safe now?

18:24.060 --> 18:25.310
Is it true?

18:24.820 --> 18:25.540
Hevee?

18:25.540 --> 18:26.500
Is it safe to come out?

18:26.500 --> 18:27.170
Director?

18:27.170 --> 18:28.040
Hevee?

18:29.820 --> 18:31.950
You saved all these people?

18:39.100 --> 18:40.940
I apologize, Hevee.

18:41.430 --> 18:43.810
I judged you too soon.

18:43.810 --> 18:45.170
Pay it no mind.

18:45.170 --> 18:48.310
Oh, but I do. And I owe you thanks.

18:48.310 --> 18:50.890
Please accept my apology, 
and name your reward.

18:50.890 --> 18:54.180
Very well, those boots 
you're currently wearing.

18:54.690 --> 18:57.710
<i>Ayep, so much for reevaluations.</i>

19:01.190 --> 19:03.790
<i>When we brought the survivors 
back to the village,</i>

19:03.790 --> 19:06.520
<i>there were joyous reunions 
to be seen here and there.</i>

19:08.140 --> 19:09.080
Take them.

19:09.080 --> 19:13.410
I accept, along with the 
sultry scent of your feet.

19:13.410 --> 19:16.100
Oh, I can feel the history.

19:18.460 --> 19:20.850
But please, rest assured.

19:20.850 --> 19:25.100
You yourself are not my type or anything.
I just want the boots.

19:26.470 --> 19:28.970
I see you're still sick in the head.

19:28.970 --> 19:34.100
I'm glad to have our healer again, 
but I can't say I'm thrilled.

19:34.460 --> 19:37.270
Here are your boots back, Director.

19:37.270 --> 19:39.630
No, I can't go back on my word.

19:39.630 --> 19:40.360
You sure?

19:40.360 --> 19:42.500
If you give this guy footwear...

19:46.110 --> 19:47.460
What'll happen?

19:47.460 --> 19:50.700
<i>I'm curious, but it's just 
as well I don't know.</i>

19:50.700 --> 19:53.730
He is great at what he does, though.

19:53.730 --> 19:56.960
That's right, Aka. He's saved 
our hides several times.

19:56.960 --> 19:59.820
You two have always put 
up with Hevee's antics.

19:59.820 --> 20:01.810
Yeah, because why not?

20:01.810 --> 20:05.970
But it's sure been a while since this many 
of the Menagerie of Fools were together.

20:02.510 --> 20:05.970
<b>The Menagerie of Fools</b>

20:05.970 --> 20:07.070
That's true.

20:07.070 --> 20:11.230
You're all such free spirits, 
it makes it hard to lead.

20:11.230 --> 20:14.120
Stare...

20:12.240 --> 20:15.550
What's with those,
"You're one to talk" looks?

20:16.100 --> 20:20.710
<i>Hevee has his flaws, but he's 
apparently a great help in battle.</i>

20:20.710 --> 20:23.470
<i>Adding a healer to the mix is a big deal.</i>

20:25.010 --> 20:28.310
Might I have some warm tea?

20:28.310 --> 20:29.240
<i>Hello there.</i>

20:29.950 --> 20:33.200
Hmm, all these products 
are unfamiliar to me.

20:33.200 --> 20:35.990
I do believe Lammis recommended...

20:36.340 --> 20:37.750
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

20:40.860 --> 20:41.880
<i>W-a-i-t.</i>

20:41.880 --> 20:44.190
Oh? Is something amiss?

20:44.190 --> 20:47.060
<i>I can tell by looking, 
that's a boot! Not a cup!</i>

20:47.060 --> 20:50.960
Could it be you're worried 
about this leaking?

20:50.960 --> 20:54.560
Fear not. There is in fact a cup inside.

20:55.070 --> 20:56.330
<i>That makes sense.</i>

20:56.330 --> 20:57.260
<i>No, it doesn't!</i>

20:57.260 --> 21:00.430
By the way, this boot was 
worn for twelve years.

21:00.430 --> 21:02.720
Its original owner was a lady hunter,

21:02.720 --> 21:05.340
and sweat and experience 
permeate this rare gem.

21:05.340 --> 21:07.530
I did give it a good cleaning, of course.

21:07.530 --> 21:09.470
<i>That's a bit of a relief.</i>

21:09.470 --> 21:13.790
I mean, you only get about a week 
at most to enjoy the scent.

21:13.790 --> 21:15.780
<i>I take it back! He's a total pervert!</i>

21:18.620 --> 21:20.860
A talking magic item.

21:20.860 --> 21:24.290
From what I hear, you have 
a human soul inside you.

21:24.290 --> 21:25.270
<i>Y-ea.</i>

21:26.110 --> 21:30.110
It would seem you've been saddled 
with quite the hapless fate.

21:30.110 --> 21:34.300
But perhaps you should be a bit 
more easygoing about things.

21:34.310 --> 21:35.810
<b>Early Afternoon Tea</b>

21:36.120 --> 21:39.980
You're so tense, you're hard as a rock.

21:40.360 --> 21:42.300
<i>Thank you.</i>

21:42.300 --> 21:45.260
I was hoping for a laugh, 
moreso than thanks.

21:45.260 --> 21:47.750
Well, you only live once.

21:47.750 --> 21:50.170
Might as well do the things you want to do.

21:50.940 --> 21:54.110
Also, it's hard to say why,

21:54.110 --> 21:59.500
but I sense in you the same special 
hobbyist spirit that I possess.

21:59.500 --> 22:01.240
<i>N-o you d-o-n-t.</i>

22:01.560 --> 22:04.730
<i>I'll deny that with my dying beep!</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:37.040
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Respective Wishes</b>

23:37.920 --> 23:40.210
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
